# Database schema (nwk1 + apollo + SST port)

No in-repo `CREATE TABLE` for nwk1 `company`/`locations` — columns reconstructed from PHP. Apollo ETL types from SST Postgres port of MySQL dumps: `projects/bbi-sst/migrations/20260709120000_001_legacy_apollo_tables.ts`.

| Engine | Host | Database |
|---|---|---|
| MySQL/MariaDB | nwk1 `127.0.0.1:3306` | `bbi_system` (`new/config/db.inc`) |
| MySQL | apollo `127.0.0.1:3306` (`:13306` on LAN) | `dominos` (`pulse_fetch/core/config.inc`) |
| Postgres | AWS RDS (SST) | port of apollo tables + `mailing_addresses` |

Do not copy DB passwords from `db.inc` / `config.inc`.

## Correlations

```
bbi_system.company.id  ←  locations.loc_comp_id
locations.location_number  ↔  daily_polling.store_number
                           ↔  MassMail_RAW.store_number
                           ↔  OR2_Raw.Location_Code
polling_processes.(fid,lid)  =  daily_polling.id range
MassMail_RAW.(store_number, CustomerProfileID, Street)
        ↔  mailing_addresses.(store_number, pulse_profile_id, old_address)   [SST]
NewCustomers.late_matched  ↔  LateCustomers.new_matched
```

**`company.rd_available`:** `0` pending data-release; `1` Domino’s Pulse; `2` alternate; `3` Vocelli (`client.inc`, `api/index.php:694`, `vocelli_direct_mail.php`).

Polling seed (`new/api/index.php:694-721`): `rd_available='1'` + location `vpn_ip_address IS NOT NULL`.

