## apollo `daily_polling`

Port `001:253-266`. Apollo PHP columns:

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `id` | PK; thread ranges |
| `store_number`, `client_name`, `vpn_ip_address`, `username`, `password` | From nwk1 API (`polling.php:30`) |
| `success` | `0` pending, `1` ok, `2` fail |
| `success_time` | unix |
| `fail_reason` | credentials / GLS / download |

TRUNCATE each Sunday (`polling.php:7`). SST adds `status`, `polling_watchdog_id`, UK `(watchdog_id, store_number)`, `message`, `data_source`.

## apollo `polling_watchdog`

Port `001:367-388`. See `02-etl-state-machine.mdc` for flag transitions.

| Column | Type (port) |
|---|---|
| `id`, `start_time`, `end_time` | bigint unix; `end_time` empty until NLL ROI done |
| `process_lock` | mutex |
| `polling`, `insert_new/late/massmail/or2`, `extract_*`, `parse_*`, `scan_lapsed`, `nll_generated`, `frequent_generated`, `update_mail_roi`, `update_nll_roi` | 0/1 |

SST adds `status`, `sfn_execution_arn`, report window, store counters.

## apollo `polling_processes`

Port `001:358-364`: `fid`, `lid`, `last_activity`, `completed`. TRUNCATE each run (`polling.php:6`). Heartbeat/complete: `functions.inc:307,320`. **SST does not use this for orchestration.**

## apollo `file_list`

Port `001:324-336`. UK `(store_number, filename)`.

| Column | Apollo | SST extra |
|---|---|---|
| `dir` | `EOutbox`/`EArchive` | often unused |
| `t_read` | unix | |
| `status` | `1` downloaded, `2` fail | `1` = downloaded |
| `fail_reason` | | |
| `s3_path` | unused | S3 key |
| `ingested` / `legacy_ingested` | — | false until ingest Map |

Insert: `functions.inc:306-309`. Skip if `COUNT(*) WHERE filename=…` (`:302`).

